jia: Quick note — onboarding sampleapp hit a strange parity issue between Node & Python SDKs for embeddings + rerank. Filing here before opening full ticket.

omar: what happened?

jia: Short: Node batching helper sometimes returns extra nesting for single-item batches (e.g. [[...vec...]]) while Python returns a flat vector ([...vec...]). Also rerank responses across model rollouts used different keys (score, ranking_score, score_value). Finally saw duplicate processing when auth retry re-sent requests without our idempotency header.

rachel: Can you paste a tiny repro and the responses you saw?

jia: Yep, abbreviated: 

```
// Node sampleapp helper output
const batch = makeBatch([{text: 'find coffee'}]);
// batch -> [ [0.01, 0.02, ...] ]  // nested for n=1

// Python helper
b = make_batch(['find coffee'])
# b -> [0.01, 0.02, ...]  // flat

// Rerank examples from hosted API we observed:
{ "results": [{ "id": "doc1", "score": 0.83 }] }
{ "results": [{ "id": "doc1", "ranking_score": 0.83 }] }
{ "results": [{ "id": "doc1", "score_value": 0.83 }] }

// Auth retry trace (from logs):
[auth] 401 -> refresh -> resend w/o x-rw-idempotency-token -> server processed twice
```

omar: I can reproduce the Node nesting locally. Helper always wraps outputs then consumer wraps again in some paths. We should choose an explicit contract.

rachel: For rerank keys, SDK should normalize to `score` with fallback order: score > ranking_score > score_value > confidence. Add a JSON schema check in SDK tests to catch this.

jia: Short-term workaround I pushed to the sampleapp template: normalize embeddings to ensure list-of-list and map rerank keys before downstream logic. Snippet: 

```js
let vecs = resp.data;
if (!Array.isArray(vecs[0])) vecs = [vecs];
const mapped = res.results.map(r => ({ id: r.id, score: r.score ?? r.ranking_score ?? r.score_value ?? r.confidence }));
```
auth-bot: Created ticket DEVEX-3344: "SDK parity: embed batch shape + rerank key variance + auth retry idempotency". Please link PRs: node-batch-shape, sdk-rerank-normalize, auth-retry-idempotency.

omar: I'll open the node-batch-shape PR to make the helper always return array-of-vectors (list-of-list) and add unit tests for n=1 and n>1. Also will add a docstring to state the contract.

rachel: I'll add the SDK mapping patch and a small CI schema assertion for rerank responses. Also will add an e2e parity test in sampleapp asserting Node & Py normalized outputs match.

auth-bot: Note: auth middleware maintainers — preserve x-rw-idempotency-token across retries or attach client-generated idempotency token that is retained.

jia: Thanks — once the three PRs land we'll remove the temporary normalization shim in the sampleapp template and add a short onboarding blurb about expected shapes until the SDK release.

ci-bot: Requested tests: unit tests for node helper (n=1, n>1), sdk rerank schema test, sampleapp e2e parity comparing normalized outputs.

jia: Closing the loop here. Will link logs & sampleapp branch to DEVEX-3344 and ping when PRs reference it. :thumbsup:
